  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe algorithm https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#list-owner assumes that element has a parent, which as I understand does not hold for a shadow roots.\n\nConsider the following HTML:\n\n```html\n<todo-item></todo-item>\n<script>\n  const template = document.createElement(\"template\");\n  template.innerHTML = `<li></li>`;\n\n  class TodoItem extends HTMLElement {\n    constructor() {\n      super();\n      const shadow = this.attachShadow({ mode: \"open\" });\n      const node = document.importNode(template.content, true);\n      shadow.appendChild(node);\n    }\n  }\n\n  customElements.define(\"todo-item\", TodoItem);\n</script>\n```\n\nThe `<li>` as I understand will have no parent element, counter to the spec note:\n> Such an element will always exist, as at the very least the [document element](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element) will always produce a [CSS box](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display/#css-box).\n\nI believe the fix would likely be to remove the spec note, and add a step to early return if element has no parent.",
